  "activity": {
    "id": "act_dna_replication",
    "name": "DNA Structure and Semiconservative Replication",
    "description": "A hands-on AR exploration of the DNA double helix and its semiconservative replication. Learners identify structural components, apply complementary base-pairing rules, examine antiparallel directionality, trace the enzymes at the replication fork, distinguish leading and lagging strand synthesis, and predict daughter-molecule composition over successive rounds of replication.",
    "language": "en",
    "workplace": "wp_dna_replication_lab",
    "start": "step_structure",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "step_structure",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens_learner",
        "location": "structure_bench",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "1. The DNA Ladder: Backbones and Bases",
          "description": "Observe the schematic ladder. The two vertical lines are the sugar-phosphate backbones; each horizontal rung is a base pair. Bases are color-coded and labeled: adenine (A, red), thymine (T, blue), guanine (G, yellow), cytosine (C, green). Notice how the bases project inward from the backbones to pair with their complements. Say 'next' when ready to build the helix."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "dna_ladder",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_ladder_schematic",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "dna_ladder",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_backbone",
              "poi": "left_backbone",
              "text": "Sugar-Phosphate Backbone"
            },
            {
              "target": "dna_ladder",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_backbone",
              "poi": "right_backbone",
              "text": "Sugar-Phosphate Backbone"
            },
            {
              "target": "learner_hud",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_structure",
              "viewport": "actions"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "dna_ladder",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "learner_hud",
              "augmentation": "narration_structure"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_helix",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_helix",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_helix",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens_learner",
        "location": "structure_bench",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "2. From Ladder to Double Helix",
          "description": "Watch the flat ladder twist into the familiar double helix: the backbones spiral around a common axis while the base pairs stack along the interior. This is what real DNA looks like inside cells \u2014 one full turn about every ten base pairs. Use the toggle to switch between the schematic ladder and the realistic helix and map one representation onto the other. Say 'next' to continue."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "dna_helix",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_ladder_to_helix",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "dna_helix",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_backbone",
              "poi": "helix_center",
              "text": "Backbones spiral ~1 turn / 10 bp"
            },
            {
              "target": "learner_hud",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_helix",
              "viewport": "actions"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "dna_helix",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "learner_hud",
              "augmentation": "narration_helix"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_antiparallel",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_antiparallel",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_antiparallel",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens_learner",
        "location": "structure_bench",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "3. Antiparallel Strands and 5'-to-3' Direction",
          "description": "Directional arrows now run along each backbone \u2014 one points up, the other down. The 5' and 3' labels mark the ends of each strand, named for the carbon atoms of the sugar ring. The two strands always run in opposite directions: this antiparallel arrangement is forced by the directional chemistry of the sugar-phosphate backbone. Rotate the helix and confirm the arrows from any angle. Say 'next' to continue."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "dna_helix",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_directional_arrows",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "dna_helix",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_5prime",
              "poi": "strand_5prime_top",
              "text": "5' end"
            },
            {
              "target": "dna_helix",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_3prime",
              "poi": "strand_3prime_bottom",
              "text": "3' end"
            },
            {
              "target": "learner_hud",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_antiparallel",
              "viewport": "actions"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "dna_helix",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "learner_hud",
              "augmentation": "narration_antiparallel"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_basepairing",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_basepairing",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_basepairing",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "hololens_learner",
        "location": "structure_bench",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "4. Build the Complementary Strand",
          "description": "The left strand reads 5'-ATGCCAGT-3'; the right strand has a bare backbone. Drag loose bases from the palette to complete the complementary sequence using the base-pairing rules (A with T, G with C). Correct placements snap in and form hydrogen bonds \u2014 two dashed lines for A-T, three for G-C. The new strand runs 3'-to-5', opposite the template. Say 'next' once the strand is complete."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
